# M5 - Privacy Controls

## Status

Planned

## Goal

Introduce privacy-aware logging to safely handle sensitive information.

## Scope

- Introduce public/private value representation.
- Support automatic redaction.
- Preserve existing logging APIs.
- Keep privacy handling consistent across all log levels.

## Out of Scope

- Logger configuration.
- Multiple providers.
- Remote logging.

## Notes

Privacy should be explicit and easy to adopt without making normal logging cumbersome.

Typical usage should evolve towards:

```swift
PulseLogger.info(
    "User signed in",
    metadata: [
        "email": .private(email),
        "userId": .public(id)
    ]
)
```

Update the status on top of this file to "Done" and record important architectural decisions once implementation completes.